      ],
      "source": "https://www.trawellino.com/destinations/united-states/california_mayflower-village",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Mayflower Village was originally part of the San Gabriel Mission lands granted to settlers after Mexico secularized the missions.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.trawellino.com/destinations/united-states/california_mayflower-village",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Mayflower Village was established in the 1920s as a planned residential area designed to resemble a small town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.trawellino.com/destinations/united-states/california_mayflower-village",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Mayflower Village retains a distinct small‑town character with tree‑lined streets and historic bungalows that echo its early 20th‑century roots.",
